 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "oven wont come on"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "When an oven won't come on, it is often because the control system has reset into an automatic or timed mode—especially if there was a recent power cut—and heating is inhibited until you select 'Manual' mode. Please check if the clock was flashing; if so, set the correct time and switch the function knob to Manual (often shown as a hand symbol). If it was already in manual mode, please try turning the temperature up on a standard fan or bake setting for 15 minutes to see if any heat is produced."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "yes the clock is flashing 0.00. how do i set it? no manual"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "To set the clock, look for buttons labelled 'Clock', 'Timer', or '+' and '-' symbols. Use them to adjust the hours and minutes, then press 'Start' or 'OK' to confirm. Once the time is set, try turning the function knob to a standard setting (like Fan Bake) at 180°C for 15 minutes. Does any heat come out? If not, we may need to look further into the control system."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok found the buttons and set the time, and it came on and is heating now. is that it?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Yes, that is it. To avoid this in future, if there is a power cut and the display flashes, just reset the time and switch the function knob to 'Manual' (often marked with a hand symbol) before cooking. If it happens again or stops heating properly later, let me know."
  }
 ],
